(
  'baya-weaver','Baya Weaver','सुगरण','बया बुनकर','Ploceus philippinus','birds','songbirds','🐦',
  'Famous for its hanging retort-shaped nests woven with hundreds of knots, the Baya weaver turns monsoon grasslands into bustling bird colonies.',
  'Baya_weaver',
  '{"kingdom":"Animalia","phylum":"Chordata","class":"Aves","order":"Passeriformes","family":"Ploceidae","genus":"Ploceus","species":"P. philippinus"}'::jsonb,
  'Linnaeus, 1766.','LC','Common across the Indian subcontinent',
  'Length 15 cm; wingspan 6.5–7 cm',15,0.028,'Omnivore',
  ARRAY['Grass seeds','Rice grains','Insects','Nectar'],'Breeding males weave pendant nests with 200+ knots; females inspect and reject unfinished nests.',
  4,8,ARRAY['Grassland','Farmland','Wetland'],ARRAY['Asia'],ARRAY['India','Sri Lanka','Myanmar','Thailand','Indonesia'],
  '[{"label":"Breeding","value":"Monsoon, June–September"},{"label":"Clutch","value":"2–4 eggs"},{"label":"Nest","value":"Hanging flask woven by the male"}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"Social structure","value":"Colonial nesters in palms and thorn trees"},{"label":"Weaving","value":"One nest takes about 18 days and 500 trips"},{"label":"Female choice","value":"Females pick the best-built nest, not the loudest singer"}]'::jsonb,
  'Diurnal','24 km/h',
  ARRAY['Nest tree loss','Pesticides'],
  'Protected in most Indian states; nest trees along village ponds are vital.',
  ARRAY['A baya nest can have more than 500 individual grass strips.','Males turn golden-yellow on the crown only in breeding season.','Weaver birds tie knots that hold for years without glue.','Colonies often return to the same tree for decades.'],
  ARRAY['house-sparrow','common-myna','sarus-crane'],ARRAY['india','weaver','monsoon','colonial'],66
