(
  'great-hornbill','Great Hornbill','धनेश','धनेश','Buceros bicornis','birds','tropical-birds','🦅',
  'The largest Indian hornbill — a 1.3-metre fruit-eating giant with a massive yellow casque whose wingbeats can be heard 500 metres away.',
  'Great_hornbill',
  '{"kingdom":"Animalia","phylum":"Chordata","class":"Aves","order":"Bucerotiformes","family":"Bucerotidae","genus":"Buceros","species":"B. bicornis"}'::jsonb,
  'Linnaeus, 1758. State bird of Kerala and Arunachal Pradesh.','VU','Fewer than 50,000, declining',
  'Length 95–130 cm; wingspan 151 cm',130,3.25,'Frugivore',
  ARRAY['Wild figs','Forest fruits','Small mammals','Insects','Nestlings fed fruit and lizards'],'Signed the formal description from Sri Lankan and Malabar specimens; disperses the biggest seeds of any Indian bird.',
  35,50,ARRAY['Rainforest','Deciduous forest'],ARRAY['Asia'],ARRAY['India','Nepal','Bhutan','Myanmar','Thailand','Indonesia'],
  '[{"label":"Nesting","value":"Large tree hollows, female sealed inside"},{"label":"Clutch","value":"1–2 eggs"},{"label":"Incubation","value":"38–40 days; female depends entirely on the male"}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"Social structure","value":"Monogamous pairs"},{"label":"Wingbeats","value":"Whooshing audible hundreds of metres away"},{"label":"Seed dispersal","value":"Key disperser of large-seeded rainforest trees"}]'::jsonb,
  'Diurnal','40 km/h',
  ARRAY['Deforestation of nesting trees','Hunting for casque and feathers','Low reproductive rate'],
  'Kerala''s state bird; community hornbill monitoring in the Western Ghats protects nest trees.',
  ARRAY['The female walls herself into a tree hollow for three months while the male feeds her.','Its massive casque amplifies calls like a resonance chamber.','Wingbeat whoosh can be heard 500 m away in still forest.','It swallows fruits up to 5 cm wide whole.'],
  ARRAY['indian-grey-hornbill','southern-birdwing','aslian-koel'],ARRAY['india','western ghats','rainforest','vulnerable','state bird'],74
