(
  'house-crow','House Crow','कावळा','कौवा','Corvus splendens','birds','songbirds','🐦',
  'The grey-necked urban survivor of South Asia — among the most intelligent birds, using traffic as a nutcracker and cities as its empire.',
  'House_crow',
  '{"kingdom":"Animalia","phylum":"Chordata","class":"Aves","order":"Passeriformes","family":"Corvidae","genus":"Corvus","species":"C. splendens"}'::jsonb,
  'Vieillot, 1817.','LC','Abundant; expanding along coasts worldwide',
  'Length 40 cm; wingspan 60–70 cm',40,0.3,'Omnivore',
  ARRAY['Food scraps','Insects','Eggs and chicks','Fruit','Grain'],'A bold generalist that learns fast; uses tools, follows ploughs and drops nuts onto roads.',
  14,20,ARRAY['Urban','Farmland','Coastal'],ARRAY['Asia','Africa'],ARRAY['India','Bangladesh','Sri Lanka','Nepal','Yemen'],
  '[{"label":"Clutch","value":"3–6 eggs"},{"label":"Incubation","value":"15–17 days"},{"label":"Nest","value":"Stick platform in trees or on buildings"}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"Intelligence","value":"Solves puzzles and uses objects as tools"},{"label":"Social structure","value":"Family groups; joint defence against hawks"},{"label":"Voice","value":"A sharp, nasal kao-kao"}]'::jsonb,
  'Diurnal','50 km/h',
  ARRAY['Persecution as a nuisance','City habitat cleaning'],
  'Tolerated widely; keep it as an urban scavenger rather than poisoning.',
  ARRAY['House crows use cars to crack hard food items.','They recognise individual human faces and remember grudges.','They mob owls and hawks in organised groups.','An invasive house crow population reached East Africa and Europe aboard ships.'],
  ARRAY['common-myna','red-vented-bulbul','asian-koel'],ARRAY['urban','intelligent','corvid','india'],60
