  '{"kingdom":"Animalia","phylum":"Chordata","class":"Aves","order":"Piciformes","family":"Picidae","genus":"Dinopium","species":"D. benghalense"}'::jsonb,
  'Linnaeus, 1758.','LC','Widespread over the subcontinent',
  'Length 26–29 cm; wingspan ~40 cm',28,0.08,'Insectivore',
  ARRAY['Ants','Wood-boring beetle larvae','Termites','Flower nectar'],'Hammers bark to expose grubs; its shock-absorbing skull takes 20 strikes a second.',
  6,12,ARRAY['Deciduous forest','Urban','Farmland'],ARRAY['Asia'],ARRAY['India','Sri Lanka','Pakistan','Nepal','Bangladesh'],
  '[{"label":"Nest","value":"Excavated cavity in a tree trunk"},{"label":"Clutch","value":"2–4 white eggs"},{"label":"Incubation","value":"14–15 days"}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"Drumming","value":"Rolls on resonant deadwood to proclaim territory"},{"label":"Tongue","value":"Sticky barbed tongue extends 5 cm beyond the beak"},{"label":"Feet","value":"Zygodactyl grip plus stiff tail prop"}]'::jsonb,
  'Diurnal','—',
  ARRAY['Deadwood removal','Nesting-tree loss'],
  'Leave standing dead trees in orchards; flamebacks control wood pests.',
  ARRAY['Its skull contains spongy bone that cushions every peck.','Woodpecker saliva is antiseptic and kills wood fungi.','A flameback can drum more than 1,200 times in one session.','Called sutaar pakshi — carpenter bird — in Marathi.'],
  ARRAY['common-kingfisher','baya-weaver'],ARRAY['woodpecker','india','drumming','cavity nester'],62
